 "notes": "The finalist is the final ARS parameter mean after 12 updates (no checkpoint selection, no fallback), frozen and hashed in finalist.json before any confirmation case; confirmation is the established evaluator (one whole 128-case manifest per fresh process, reference then finalist), twelve manifests on seeds 4780-4791 never used before. Deviation (recorded in amendment_r106_smoke.json before any training, advisor consult call_00235, decision delegated by the user): the first smoke (seed 4778, 8,204 starts) failed on two defects in the implementer's new child: the scorer required 360 recorded steps for a completed episode (a time-out episode has 359), scoring every episode a failure, and a duplicate-slot check demanded bit identity across environments. Both were fixed (scorer = cases.sustained on the episode's own length, with an equivalence test; tolerance 1e-4, measured 6.4e-6), the smoke was rerun once on new seed 4792 and passed every gate, and the ceiling was raised from 115,000 to 125,000 starts including the failed attempt; 120,972 were charged. A/A yardstick (identical zero-theta policy, identical 512 placements, four slots of one batch): slot success 0.465/0.465/0.459/0.459, pairwise case discordance 0.074-0.104, SD of slot differences 0.003: a 512-case training contrast between two candidates in one batch is far less noisy than two fresh processes would suggest. Training-time candidate success rose from about 0.36-0.47 (update 1) to 0.50-0.56 (update 12) on different placements each update; that drift is not the evidence, the fresh confirmation is. The interval shows a positive effect and its lower bound (+0.079) is above +0.05. Scope: one ARS trajectory, one residual family; it does not show ARS beats PPO or draws given the same objective and budget, nor that the exact-success objective (rather than the 38x larger training budget and 512 shared cases per candidate) is the cause; R-103's arms had 460,800 transitions each, this run 17.6 M. The saved incumbent asset is unchanged. The finalist has no reference slot in training, so 'training rejected' was not an available outcome by design."
